+**This repository gates categories 5-8 on measurement.** Categories 1-4
+(`async-`, `bundle-`, `server-`, `client-`) are structural: they remove round
+trips and shipped bytes, so apply them by default. Categories 5-8 (`rerender-`,
+`rendering-`, `js-`, `advanced-`) trade certain readability for uncertain gain,
+so apply them only where a measurement identifies the hot path, and record the
+before/after numbers.
+
+`docs/repository/code-design.md#performance` is authoritative here and states two
+explicit non-rules that override individual entries below: there is no blanket
+ban on `map`/`filter`/`reduce` (against `js-combine-iterations` and
+`js-flatmap-filter`), and no blanket memoization (against `rerender-memo`). A
+performance change without a measurement is a guess.
+
